Feature: Calculate Total Time Elapsed (TAT) for New Enrollment Review Activity

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the tables "pat_case" and "sr_activity" exist in the schema
    And the "pat_case" table has columns "case_id", "service_request_type", and "sr_created_date"
    And the "sr_activity" table has columns "case_id", "subject", "status", and "last_modified_date"

  Scenario Outline: Calculate TAT for New Enrollment Review Activity
    Given the "pat_case" table has a row with "service_request_type" = "Patient Foundation" and "sr_created_date" = "<start_date>"
    And the "sr_activity" table has a row with "subject" = "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity", "status" = "Completed", and "last_modified_date" = "<end_date>" for the same "case_id"
    When the TAT calculation is performed
    Then the "total_time_elapsed" is calculated as "<end_date>" - "<start_date>" (date only) and adjusted for weekends
    And the result is loaded into the "tat_report" table with all columns from the "pat_case" table

  Examples:
    | start_date  | end_date    | total_time_elapsed |
    | 2022-01-01  | 2022-01-05  | 4                   |
    | 2022-01-01  | 2022-01-01  | 0                   |
    | 2022-01-05  | 2022-01-01  | NULL                |
    | NULL        | 2022-01-05  | NULL                |
    | 2022-01-01  | NULL        | NULL                |

  Scenario: Handle invalid dates
    Given the "pat_case" table has a row with "service_request_type" = "Patient Foundation" and "sr_created_date" = "invalid_date"
    And the "sr_activity" table has a row with "subject" = "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity", "status" = "Completed", and "last_modified_date" = "2022-01-05" for the same "case_id"
    When the TAT calculation is performed
    Then the "total_time_elapsed" is NULL
    And an error message is logged "Invalid date format for sr_created_date"

  Scenario: Handle missing data
    Given the "pat_case" table has a row with "service_request_type" = "Patient Foundation" and "sr_created_date" = "2022-01-01"
    And the "sr_activity" table does not have a row with "subject" = "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" and "status" = "Completed" for the same "case_id"
    When the TAT calculation is performed
    Then the "total_time_elapsed" is NULL
    And an error message is logged "No matching row found in sr_activity table"
